From c38a532b740071e7a96145ec6422e8f5057a1d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Barry Song (Xiaomi)" <baohua@kernel.org>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:47:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] mm: move folio_lock_or_retry() to memory.c

folio_lock_or_retry() is used only by fault paths in mm/memory.c.  Move
it there and make it static so the generic pagemap interface no longer
exposes a fault-specific helper.

Fold __folio_lock_or_retry() into folio_lock_or_retry() while moving it.
This also gives the swap fault path a local place for the short-wait
policy added by the next patch.

Signed-off-by: Barry Song (Xiaomi) <baohua@kernel.org>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260430040427.4672-4-baohua@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
---
 include/linux/pagemap.h | 17 ------------
 mm/filemap.c            | 45 ------------------------------
 mm/memory.c             | 61 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 66 deletions(-)

